  "question": {
    "text": "A galvanometer has a current range of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math> and a voltage range of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>750</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mV</mi></math>. To convert this galvanometer into an ammeter of range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>,&nbsp;the required shunt is"
